    "diagnosis": "Osteochondroma formation",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "A second hit in EXT in a proliferating cell of the growth plate near the bony collar underlies osteochondroma formation in patients with multiple osteochondromas. The cells lose polarity and grow out of the bone through a defective bony collar. In the cartilaginous cap, EXT&minus;/&minus; cells are intermingled with EXT+/&minus; cells (mosaicism). In solitary osteochondromas, two somatic hits are required in a single chondrocyte.",
